.TH OLLAMA\-MESH-NODE 1 "2026-08-17" "ollama-mesh dev" "ollama-mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
ollama\-mesh-node \- node control driver operations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ollama\-mesh node
[action] [args] [\fIflags\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
node control driver operations
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B control
show or accept a node's control driver
.TP
.B control probe <node>
show a node's control\-driver status (configured + discovered)
.TP
.B control accept <node>
accept a control driver + identifier for a node
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-driver string
control driver: systemd, docker, process, launchd, or windows_service (required)
.TP
.B \-\-identifier string
driver\-specific identifier (unit name, container name, PID file path, plist label, service name) (required)
.TP
.B \-\-start-command string
launch command for the process driver's Start action (only meaningful when \-\-driver=process)
.RE
.SH FLAGS
.TP
.B \-\-server
Admin API base URL (default "http://localhost:8080", env MESH_SERVER)
.TP
.B \-\-json
output machine\-readable JSON instead of a human table
.TP
.B \-\-username
admin username, used to log in (env MESH_USERNAME)
.TP
.B \-\-password
admin password, used to log in (env MESH_PASSWORD)
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBollama\-mesh\fR(1)
